  "tagline": "Young C storage-engine library: transactional LSM with MVCC, column families and TTL.",
  "description": "TidesDB is a transactional key-value storage engine library written in C, built on a hybrid LSM-tree/B-tree design with MVCC, column families, key-value separation and a configurable compression pipeline (Snappy, LZ4, Zstd). It offers several isolation levels including two-phase-commit XA, TTLs, range deletes and bloom filters, and it runs on a wide range of operating systems and CPU architectures. The project launched in 2024, iterates fast (major version 10 by late 2026) and is licensed under MPL-2.0. It is promising for people building their own databases but lacks the production history of RocksDB.",
